-- Magna Carta (1215), English translation in McKechnie 1905: CHAPTERS 20 TO 22.
-- Amercements: of freemen, merchants and villeins (20), of earls and barons (21) and of clerks (22).
-- Terms the text does not define, taken as plain facts or typed values (see NOTES.md):
-- amerced, "fallen into our mercy", contenement, wainage, villein, honest men of the
-- neighbourhood, peers, clerk, lay holding, church benefice, degree and gravity of an offence.
-- The text names no one who amerces (it speaks of falling "into our mercy"), so these are decision
